l","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=518554&INSPECTION_NN=518554","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"491744","date":"2024-02-23","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=491744&INSPECTION_NN=491744","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"483951","date":"2023-12-11","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=483951&INSPECTION_NN=483951","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"457949","date":"2023-05-22","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=457949&INSPECTION_NN=457949","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"443320","date":"2023-01-18","visit":"Follow-up","type_raw":"1st Re-Inspect","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=443320&INSPECTION_NN=443320","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"442941","date":"2023-01-11","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":1,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=442941&INSPECTION_NN=442941","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":16,"title":"Food-contact surfaces; cleaned and sanitized","repeat":false,"comment":"4-501.114: Chemical sanitizer for manual or mechanical operation shall meet proper criteria: (A) chlorine shall have minimum temperature (55F), concentration (100ppm), and pH (10). (B) Iodine shall have 68F, pH of 5 or less and concentration of 12.5ppm and 25ppm. (C) Quaternary ammonium shall have 75F, concentration based on label, and water with 500ppm hardness or less. (D) - (E) Meets EPA-label use and regulatory authority approval. (P) (F) Other chemical sanitzers in-use shall have EPA-registered label, display device registration number on devide and is operated and maintained in accordance with manufacturers instructions (Pf)\n\nObserved the dish machine (heat function is not working, PIC is aware and not utilizing it) to be pulling 10-50 ppm of chlorine bleach. Facility is utilizing only the bleach component for sanitizing purposes. Kohl’s will be called by PIC to service the dish machine. Multiple runs were conducted and each produced either 10-50 ppm or 0 ppm with test strips. Facility has test strips to check concentration level. Facility also has a maximum registering thermometer to check heat sanitization levels with the heat function is properly working. Inspector will follow-up on 1/17/23. This is a 3 day follow-up; however, the Inspector has prior SCDPH engagements (conference) and county issued holiday on Monday, 1/16/23. Inspector instructed facility to utilize the 3 compartment sink - wash, rinse, sanitize. Dish machine may be used to wash and rinse, sanitize must occur in the 3 compartment sink with correct bleach concentration (50-200 ppm).","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"418622","date":"2022-05-17","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":1,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=418622&INSPECTION_NN=418622","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":28,"title":"Toxic substances properly identified, stored, and used","repeat":false,"comment":"7-202.12: (A) POISONOUS MATERIALS shall be used according to LAW(C), Manufacturer’s directions (indicate for use in FOOD ESTABLISHMENT) (P), conditions of certification (if applicable) (P), and additional conditions (if applicable) (C).\n\nThe bottle of bleach used to make sani buckets in the facility does not have direction for making a solution intended for food contact surfaces.  Directions observed seem to indicate uses for laundry and bathroom use. Inspector discussed with the PIC. PIC found instructions on the internet for the making a solution intended for food contact surfaces and printed them out during the inspection to correct. Inspector reviewed label requirements with the PIC  emphasizing EPA registrations numbers and instructions for making solutions intended for sanitizing food contact surfaces.","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"410083","date":"2022-02-24","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=410083&INSPECTION_NN=410083","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"398420","date":"2021-10-06","visit":"Complaint","type_raw":"Complaint","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=398420&INSPECTION_NN=398420","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"384076","date":"2021-04-21","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=384076&INSPECTION_NN=384076","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"379503","date":"2021-02-22","visit":"Spot check","type_raw":"Spot Check","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=379503&INSPECTION_NN=379503","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"378773","date":"2021-02-08","visit":"Spot check","type_raw":"Spot Check","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=378773&INSPECTION_NN=378773","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"378425","date":"2021-02-01","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":1,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=378425&INSPECTION_NN=378425","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":16,"title":"Food-contact surfaces; cleaned and sanitized","repeat":false,"comment":"4-501.112: (A) Temperature of the fresh hot water SANITIZING rinse may not be more than 194F or less than 165F for stationary rack, single temperature machines. All other machines can be no less than 180F. (B) Maximum temperature does not apply to high pressure and temperature systems with wand-type spraying devices. \n\nInspector could not get a temperature reading in the hot water sanitizing dish machine higher than 151 degrees Fahrenheit. Multiple attempts were made using both the inspector's thermometer and the facility's (both registered within 1 degree of each other). Follow up will be set for 2/15/21. Until the machine can be verified as sanitizing effectively, the facility will use a Chlorine solution to sanitize after washing in the dish machine.","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"376016","date":"2020-12-14","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=376016&INSPECTION_NN=376016","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"371105","date":"2020-09-16","visit":"Spot check","type_raw":"Spot Check","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=371105&INSPECTION_NN=371105","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"356414","date":"2020-02-10","visit":"Follow-up","type_raw":"1st Re-Inspect","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=356414&INSPECTION_NN=356414","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"354790","date":"2020-01-27","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":1,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=354790&INSPECTION_NN=354790","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":16,"title":"Food-contact surfaces; cleaned and sanitized","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"4-501.112","citation_text":"4-501.112  (Pf) The inspector's maximum registering thermometer registered 151°-158°F in the dish machine over several attempts. The critical limit for temperature based sanitizing is 160°F. Maintenance was contacted during the inspection. The follow up is set for February 10, 2020."}]},{"id":"330130","date":"2019-04-29","visit":"Spot check","type_raw":"Spot Check","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=330130&INSPECTION_NN=330130","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"329868","date":"2019-04-25","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":1,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=329868&INSPECTION_NN=329868","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":16,"title":"Food-contact surfaces; cleaned and sanitized","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"4-501.112","citation_text":"4-501.112 (A) The temperature of the fresh hot water SANITIZING rinse as it enters the manifold may not be more than 194F, or less than 180F.\nThe dish machine was only registering approximately 160F at the manifold and was not registering at safe sanitizing temperatures on the inspector's maximum registering test strip. Maintenance was called and began work on the machine during the inspection. A follow up is set for 10 business days (5/9/19). The machine was switched to chemical sanitizing during the inspection to continue operation."}]},{"id":"321712","date":"2019-01-25","visit":"Spot check","type_raw":"Spot Check","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=321712&INSPECTION_NN=321712","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"321185","date":"2019-01-23","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8451&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=321185&INSPECTION_NN=321185","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"273342","date":"2018-04-24","visit":"Routine","type_r